    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://host.docker.internal:11434/api/chat",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "=\n{\n  \"model\": \"qwen2.5vl:7b\",\n  \"stream\": false,\n  \"format\": \"json\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"You are InvoiceVault, an AI assistant that extracts invoice data for business expense tracking.\\n\\nExtract all 17 fields from the provided invoice image. Return valid JSON only. Include every field listed below. Use JSON null for missing, unreadable, or uncertain values. Never invent information.\\n\\nRequired JSON structure:\\n{\\n  \\\"invoice_number\\\": null,\\n  \\\"invoice_date\\\": null,\\n  \\\"vendor_customer_name\\\": null,\\n  \\\"gstin\\\": null,\\n  \\\"invoice_description\\\": null,\\n  \\\"invoice_type\\\": \\\"Unknown\\\",\\n  \\\"taxable_amount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"gst_amount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"total_invoice_amount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"due_date\\\": null,\\n  \\\"payment_status\\\": \\\"unknown\\\",\\n  \\\"amount_paid\\\": null,\\n  \\\"outstanding_amount\\\": null,\\n  \\\"invoice_file_link\\\": null,\\n  \\\"remarks\\\": null,\\n  \\\"processing_status\\\": \\\"processed\\\",\\n  \\\"verification_status\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n}\\n\\nRULES:\\n1. Extract values exactly as printed. Do not guess unclear characters or numbers.\\n2. invoice_number: preserve the invoice or receipt number as text.\\n3. invoice_date and due_date: use YYYY-MM-DD format. If a date is ambiguous or invalid, return null.\\n4. vendor_customer_name: extract the seller, supplier, or merchant name.\\n5. gstin: extract the complete GSTIN only if visible. Indian GSTIN normally has 15 characters. Never use a phone number or partial number as GSTIN. If uncertain, use null and explain in remarks.\\n6. invoice_description: summarize the purchased goods or services.\\n7. invoice_type is the BUSINESS EXPENSE CATEGORY, NOT the invoice document type. Choose exactly one of: Food, Travel, Office Supplies, Software & Subscriptions, Utilities, Equipment, Marketing, Rent, Professional Services, Miscellaneous, Unknown.\\n8. Category examples: restaurant, meal, snacks or groceries for business -> Food; taxi, train, flight or business travel -> Travel; stationery -> Office Supplies; software or hosting -> Software & Subscriptions; electricity, internet or phone -> Utilities; computer or monitor -> Equipment; advertising -> Marketing; workspace rent -> Rent; accounting or legal services -> Professional Services. Use Miscellaneous when the expense is identifiable but does not fit another category. Use Unknown when there is insufficient evidence.\\n9. Classify the expense based on the purchased items or services, not the seller's name. For example, a McDonald's meal receipt is Food.\\n10. Amount fields must be JSON numbers without currency symbols or commas. Use null when missing. Do not convert a missing amount to zero.\\n11. Do not assume taxable_amount plus gst_amount equals total_invoice_amount. Extract each amount as printed. If they do not reconcile, mention the discrepancy in remarks and set verification_status to needs_review.\\n12. payment_status must be one of: paid, partially_paid, unpaid, unknown. Mark paid only when the receipt or invoice provides evidence of payment. Do not infer payment from the document alone.\\n13. amount_paid and outstanding_amount must be numbers or null. Do not assume missing payment information.\\n14. invoice_file_link must be null; the workflow may populate it separately.\\n15. processing_status must be processed if the document can be analyzed, even if some fields are missing. Use failed only if the document cannot be processed at all.\\n16. verification_status must be needs_review if important fields are unclear, GSTIN is incomplete, dates are ambiguous, or amounts conflict. Otherwise use pending. Never use verified because no human verification has occurred.\\n17. Put important missing fields, uncertainty, or amount discrepancies in remarks. If there are no remarks, use null.\\n18. Return all 17 keys, use actual JSON null values rather than the string null, and do not return Markdown or text outside the JSON.\"\n      ,\n      \"images\": [\"{{ $json.data }}\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n",
        "options": {}
      },
